    "content": "The Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) has reiterated its backing for the unity, independence, and territorial integrity of the Federal Republic of Somalia. The affirmation came during a meeting between Somalia's Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Absalan Ali, and the OIC Secretary-General, Ismael Ould Cheikh Ahmed, held in the Iraqi capital, Baghdad. The meeting took place on the sidelines of the 52nd session of the OIC Council of Foreign Ministers.\n\nThe discussions focused on the ongoing cooperation between Somalia and the OIC, with the Secretary-General emphasizing the organization's continued support for Somalia's sovereignty and territorial integrity. The two officials also reviewed the progress made by the Somali government in various sectors, including security, development, and regional stability. The OIC has historically been a key partner for Somalia, providing political and humanitarian support.\n\nThis reaffirmation comes at a critical time for Somalia, as the country continues to navigate complex regional dynamics and internal challenges. The OIC's stance is seen as a diplomatic boost for the federal government's efforts to maintain national unity and territorial integrity. The meeting also provided an opportunity for Somalia to highlight its priorities and seek further collaboration with the OIC and its member states.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the OIC's support is significant as it underscores international recognition of Somalia's sovereignty and the legitimacy of its federal institutions. Many diaspora members are actively involved in Somalia's reconstruction and development, and such diplomatic backing can enhance their confidence in the country's stability and future. Moreover, the OIC's engagement with Somalia often translates into tangible support for humanitarian and development projects that benefit diaspora-led initiatives.\n\nThe meeting in Baghdad is part of a broader diplomatic engagement by Somalia to strengthen ties with international partners and garner support for its national priorities. The Somali government has been actively participating in international forums to advocate for its sovereignty and to attract investment and assistance. The OIC's repeated affirmations of support are expected to reinforce Somalia's position in the international community.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/17/oic-oo-mar-kale-xaqiijisay-taageerada-midnimada-iyo-wadajirka-dhuleed-ee-soomaaliya/",
