    "content": "The international police organization INTERPOL has registered 34 individuals suspected of involvement in terrorism-related crimes in Bosaso, the commercial hub of Somalia's Puntland region. The registration took place during a joint operation involving INTERPOL, the Puntland Marine Police Force (PMPF), and Somali security agencies, according to a report by Goobjoog.\n\nThe operation focused on improving the use of fingerprint identification data and enhancing the sharing of intelligence information among the participating agencies. During the exercise, an INTERPOL expert provided technical support, though the source did not specify the expert's full role or the duration of the operation.\n\nThe move comes amid ongoing efforts by Puntland authorities to counter al-Shabaab and other militant groups that have targeted Bosaso and other parts of the region. Puntland has previously collaborated with international partners on counterterrorism initiatives, but the registration of suspects through INTERPOL's systems marks a step toward integrating local investigations with global law enforcement databases.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the development is significant because many diaspora members maintain close family and business ties to Bosaso. Enhanced fingerprint and intelligence-sharing mechanisms could affect diaspora members who travel to or invest in the region, as security screenings may become more thorough. Additionally, the operation signals a growing emphasis on evidence-based prosecutions, which may improve accountability and reduce the risk of wrongful detentions that have sometimes concerned diaspora communities.\n\nThe registration of suspects does not constitute a formal charge or conviction; under Somali and international law, those registered are presumed innocent until proven guilty in a competent court. It remains unclear whether the 34 individuals are in custody or whether the registration is part of a broader effort to build cases for future prosecution. Goobjoog's report did not provide further details on the suspects' identities or status.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/17/interpol-oo-diiwaangelisay-34-qof-oo-looga-shakisan-yahay-falal-argagixiso-magaalada-boosaaso/",
